G5543.d:
χρηστός, -ή, -όν
 (χράομαι), [in LXX chiefly for טוֹב (frequently of God: Ps.25:8, al.), also for יָקָר (Eze.27:22 28:13), יָשָׁר (Pro.2:21 א A) ;] 
serviceable, good; 
  (a) of things, good, pleasant: of food (as often in cl.), οἶνος, Luke.5:39; ζυγός, Matt.11:30 (EV, easy); in ethical sense, ἤθη, 1 Cor.15:33; 
  (b) of persons, good, kind, gracious: Eph.4:32; of God, Luke.6:35, 1 Pet.2:3; τ. χρηστὸν (= ἡ χρηστότης) τοῦ θεοῦ, Rom.2:4.
 † (AS)

